sub:assertion {
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0> pk:hasAssessment <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/assessment/morphoeval-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0-overall> a pk:LLMClaimAssessment ;
        rdfs:label "Drosophila silvestris Turing wavenumber at 2.995 µm (Holocene, 0 Ma) — MorphoEval overall 81.4/100" ;
        dct:date "2026-10-27"^^xsd:date ;
        dct:description "Pass 1. Schnakenberg kinetics on a periodic 8-wavelength patch with lambda_c = 2.995e-6 m at gamma = 1 and diffusivity ratio 20. The Kilohana CC BY-SA voucher is the species image. The linearised sweep matched closed-form k_c with Pearson r = 0.9894, but the wavelength correlation was 0.9878 because the peak snapped to a single Fourier mode. The dark-pixel mask had 139 components and covered the body, not just wing spots. Equal diffusion was stable (sigma_max = -0.586). This slot does not claim that the photographed wing spots are a 3 µm Turing pattern (Gompel et al. 2005). Overall 81.4/100 (faithfulness 78.7, reproducibility 87.6); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 0dc967f22ddaa01ca809b3701e8da57313f6c44d; environment: python 3.12.3, note numpy, scipy, Pillow, matplotlib. No ~/.nanopub/profile.yml on this runner.. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 86, Morphological realism / specimen match 74, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 76, Source and data traceability 90, Code-to-model traceability 84, Reproducibility package 88. Output judged: docs/media/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_comparison.png: rendered output of models/2026-delphi10000-drosophila-silvestris-turing-wavelength-s0.py at 0dc967f22ddaa01ca809b3701e8da57313f6c44d, image/png, 594499 B, 1248×984 px, artifact_sha256 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5 (sha256 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5), spec_fingerprint 94f67ddc05494c16449850f8c780e88f2c89119a3224682e596b88bad888be9c. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: 94f67ddc05494c16449850f8c780e88f2c89119a3224682e596b88bad888be9c; artifact_sha256: 0830930fc3e69be615317c86b3b6990518c90e2e1cecc6399d8126140993dfe5; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_reference.json=9f4f77b1d9bee8df..., datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0_specimen.jpg=dd93694218361504..., datasets/drosophila_silvestris_turing_wavelength_s0/paper_citations.bib=4ff27448f5d20b31...}. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Turing (1952) gives the diffusion-driven instability and a critical wavenumber. Schnakenberg (1979) gives the two-species kinetics used here. | Carson & Bryant (1979) report a mean of 20-30 extra tibial cilia in northeast Hawaiian D. silvestris males, absent in D. heteroneura. They do not report a 3 µm wavelength. | Gompel et al. (2005) attribute macroscopic Drosophila wing spots to cis-regulatory evolution.; reconstructed_in_script: Detail-tier wavelength 2.995e-6 m (log10 = -5.524), diffusivity ratio 20, and the chronoseries contrast with D. serrata (9.226e-5 m) and D. simulans (8.256e-5 m) are assigned for this slot and reconstructed from the dispersion relation. | Pass-1 readout is the single loudest Fourier mode of the linearised PDE. Pass-1 mask is every dark foreground pixel.; transfer_boundary: The wavenumber comparison is a scale contrast inside one chronoseries. It does not say that D. serrata or D. simulans evolved into D. silvestris, and it does not transfer to embryonic pair-rule stripes.; does_not_claim: Does not claim the Kilohana wing spots, or the 20-30 extra tibial cilia, are produced by a 2.995 µm Schnakenberg pattern. | Does not claim a second assessor scored this pass. Signing keys were not present.." ;
        dct:subject <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
        pk:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> ;
        pk:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
        pk:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: R1. Replace the argmax Fourier peak with a power-weighted centroid so wavelength Pearson r clears 0.98 (pass-1 lambda r = 0.9878, k r = 0.9894).",
            "remediation needed: R2. Restrict the pigment mask to dorsal wing-band islands. The pass-1 raw dark mask had 139 components and painted the body.",
            "remediation needed: R3. Make the GIF terminal frame the unmodified voucher. The pass-1 caption band left last-frame orientation KS at 0.153.",
            "remediation needed: R4. Report the nonlinear onset wavenumber against closed-form k_c, not only the linearised sweep." ;
        pk:hasScore "0.814"^^xsd:double ;
        pk:hasVerdict "faithful" .
    <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/model/grok-4.7> a pk:Model ;
        rdfs:label "Grok 4.7 (builder-assessor)" ;
        dct:identifier "grok-4.7" ;
        prov:actedOnBehalfOf <https://orcid.org/0009-0007-4948-9192> .
}

